  "diagnosis": "The candidate's transition_state function directly modifies the input state dictionary by reassigning state[\"status\"] = event. This causes the input state to be mutated, which violates the requirement that state inputs should be immutable. The training evidence shows a failure where the original state was expected to be {\"status\": \"pending\", \"count\": 1} but was altered to {\"status\": \"pending\", \"count\": 1} (the same value) because the function doesn't properly handle state immutability.",
  "expected_effect": "The function should return a new state dictionary with the updated status field without modifying the original state.",
  "schema_version": "exp002-diagnosis-update/v1",
  "updates": {
    "harness.py": "def transition_state(state, event) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return state after applying an event.\"\"\"\n    new_state = dict(state)\n    new_state[\"status\"] = event\n    return new_state"
  }
}

